f": "2026-07-17", "price": 83.0, "closing_price": 83.0}, {"as_of": "2026-07-18", "price": 83.0, "closing_price": 83.0}, {"as_of": "2026-07-19", "price": 83.0, "closing_price": 83.0}, {"as_of": "2026-07-20", "price": 83.0, "closing_price": 83.0}, {"as_of": "2026-07-21", "price": 83.1, "closing_price": 83.1}, {"as_of": "2026-07-22", "price": 80.5, "closing_price": 80.5}, {"as_of": "2026-07-23", "price": 85.0, "closing_price": 85.0}, {"as_of": "2026-07-27", "price": 84.7, "closing_price": 84.7}, {"as_of": "2026-07-28", "price": 82.9, "closing_price": 82.9}, {"as_of": "2026-07-29", "price": 82.9, "closing_price": 82.9}, {"as_of": "2026-07-30", "price": 82.8, "closing_price": 82.8}], "compare_snapshot": {"symbol": "TKYO", "company_name": "TOKYO CEMENT COMPANY (LANKA) PLC", "summary_text": "Tokyo Cement manufactures and sells cement in Sri Lanka -- the country's largest cement producer and its only listed one -- earning through volume (tonnage) x price per bag, sold through a dealer/distribution network (Annual Report 2023/24, Chairman's Message; Annual Report 2021/22, p.31). The single biggest dependency is construction-sector demand, which is itself gated by government infrastructure spending and lending rates (Annual Report 2023/24, Management Discussion and Analysis). Group revenue swung from LKR 35.8Bn (FY2020) up to LKR 56.5Bn (FY2023) and back down to LKR 49.8Bn (FY2024), tracking construction-cycle demand rather than a steady growth trend. Profitability has been considerably more volatile than revenue: FY2022 was a reported Group loss (LKR -0.36Bn) driven by a large exchange loss following the 2022 Rupee float, even though revenue grew 22% that year (Annual Report 2021/22, Chairman's Message) -- a clear illustration of currency/import-cost exposure sitting on top of the underlying cement business.", "gaps_note": "FY2025 (year ended 31 March 2025) not included: the FY2025 annual report exists in the document library (collected live, source_id 51996) but was not read for this pilot summary. The most recent interim report on file (period ended 31 December 2025) is an image-based PDF with no extractable text layer, so its figures could not be pulled automatically -- flagged here rather than estimated. FY2019 figures were visible in the FY2019/20 annual report but that report's PDF has font-encoding corruption on some numeric cells; only the unambiguous chart callouts (FY2019 Group revenue ~LKR 38.5Bn, EPS -1.23) were legible and are not included in the row-level table above to avoid citing a partially-corrupted source with false precision.", "annual": [{"period": "FY2023 (year ended 31 March 2023)", "period_end_date": "2023-03-31", "basis": "GROUP", "revenue": 56481677281.0, "operating_income": 11808474806.0, "pbt": 6772437112.0, "pat": 4998690773.0, "eps": 11.31, "currency": "LKR", "source_doc_id": "manual_0a44ac0ba47e6e18", "source_page": 104}, {"period": "FY2024 (year ended 31 March 2024)", "period_end_date": "2024-03-31", "basis": "GROUP", "revenue": 49823790136.0, "operating_income": 4887229517.0, "pbt": 3448436406.0, "pat": 2422495717.0, "eps": 5.48, "currency": "LKR", "source_doc_id": "manual_0a44ac0ba47e6e18", "source_page": 104}], "quarterly": [], "market_data": {"symbol": "TKYO", "as_of": "2026-07-30", "collected_at": "2026-07-30T19:00:26.039763", "price": 82.8, "previous_close": 82.9, "closing_price": 82.8, "open": 83.0, "high": 83.4, "low": 82.0, "turnover": 986300.5, "share_volume": 11935.0, "market_cap": 24345684000.0, "shares_outstanding": 294030000.0, "source": "tradeSummary"}, "valuation": {"price": 82.8, "market_cap": 24345684000.0, "enterprise_value": 35049308614.0, "pe_ratio": 15.109489051094888, "pb_ratio": 0.8816074051996446, "ev_ebitda": 5.468785429920058, "dividend_yield": 0.030193236714975848, "payout_ratio": 0.45620437956204374, "_gaps": []}, "ratios_annual": {"gross_profit": 15562495645.0, "gross_margin": 0.3123506983816427, "operating_margin": 0.09809027983739739, "ebitda": 6408974911.0, "ebitda_margin": 0.1286328256743603, "net_margin": 0.048621265270817574, "roe": 0.08772356378122803, "roa": 0.04784458933143612, "roce": 0.1327179881010863, "current_ratio": 1.0809410129090165, "quick_ratio": 0.669222814352004, "debt_to_equity": 0.46804843501158744, "net_debt_to_ebitda": 1.6700993158248922, "interest_coverage": 3.0547411368446626, "asset_turnover": 0.9840260031273268, "receivables_turnover": 7.1087788646788574, "working_capital": 1117668056.0, "free_cash_flow": 165535057.0, "roic": 0.08468693126083372, "roic_basis": "post-tax", "_gaps": []}, "ratios_quarterly": null, "revenue_growth_yoy": -0.1178769375398783, "pat_growth_yoy": -0.515373959500575, "thesis": {"recommendation": "HOLD", "composite_score": 51.4, "thesis_text": "Tokyo Cement is Sri Lanka's largest and only listed cement producer -- a genuine market-leadership position -- but FY2024 Group results were weak: revenue fell 11.8% and PAT fell 51.5% YoY, with leverage rising (debt/equity 0.47x, Net Debt/EBITDA up from 0.76x to 1.67x). Operating cash flow did swing positive (-7.5bn to +5.6bn), suggesting some of the earnings weakness is working-capital timing rather than a structural break, but this can't be confirmed without a more recent filing. At 15.3x trailing P/E despite the earnings decline, the stock does not look statistically cheap on an earnings basis, though its 0.89x P/B is below book (Annual Report FY2024, p.104-107)."}}}